  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "NT L-mode confinement enhancement observed on TCV/DIII-D scales favorably to burning-plasma reactor conditions (H_98 = 1.44 sustained)",
      "NT geometry's low P_SOL (5.2% of fusion power) enables a conventional tungsten monoblock divertor to handle exhaust passively, eliminating advanced divertor engineering",
      "Ohmic heating with NT confinement enhancement (H_NA ≥ 2) can achieve burning-plasma conditions without auxiliary heating, per Ball et al. 0D power balance",
      "FLiBe liquid immersion blanket achieves TBR = 1.15 with self-healing molybdenum barrier and V-4Cr-4Ti vacuum vessel compatibility at operating temperature",
      "REBCO HTS TF coils at 11 T with 40% critical-current margin survive cumulative 14 MeV neutron fluence of 3×10²² n/m² over commercial plant lifetime",
      "NT-specific vertical instability can be controlled by passive stabilizer plates (inboard plates uniquely enabled by outboard X-point migration)",
      "MANTA-class pilot economics ($3.4B overnight, $396/MWh) scale down to commercial ~$64/MWh via magnet lifetime extension, higher thermal efficiency, and ~1 GW fusion power"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Advanced divertor engineering (Super-X, snowflake, liquid metal geometries and active impurity seeding systems) — replaced by conventional tungsten monoblock at 2.8 MW/m²",
      "Auxiliary heating system capital (~$150M for 40 MW ICRF) — eliminated entirely in the ohmic-only scenario if H_NA ≥ 2 is validated",
      "ELM mitigation and H-mode pedestal control infrastructure — NT operates ELM-free in L-mode regime",
      "High-radiated-power-fraction plasma control systems (90–95% f_rad with impurity seeding) required for PT designs to reach comparable divertor heat flux",
      "Tungsten divertor replacement overhead — lower erosion rates at 2.8 MW/m² potentially extend replacement intervals from ~5 years toward ~10 years"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "NT-specific passive vertical stabilizer plate infrastructure (~$15–60M, central $30M) — absent from MANTA cost accounting and from conventional PT cost analogues",
      "NT-geometry-constrained demountable TF coil design with connection joints tailored to the NT plasma shape (18 TF coils in MANTA)",
      "FLiBe-to-NaNO₃/KNO₃ molten-salt heat exchanger at fusion-plant scale (low-TRL component called out explicitly by MANTA §6.3)",
      "Molten-salt thermal energy storage buffer sized for 15-minute pulse / 2-minute dwell quasi-steady operation",
      "V-4Cr-4Ti vacuum vessel at multi-hundred-tonne scale — no industrial supply chain exists for nuclear-grade vanadium alloy"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "NT confinement scaling to burning-plasma conditions is unvalidated; all physics data comes from non-burning L-mode experiments (TCV/DIII-D) and the H_NA, H_98, H_89 factors 'represent the biggest uncertainty' per Ball et al.",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No commercial-scale NT plant cost study exists — MANTA's 90 MWe pilot at $396/MWh is ~6× away from the ARIES-ACT $64/MWh commercial benchmark with no credible published path to close the gap",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Ohmic-only hypothesis (Q ≈ 500) depends on H_NA = 2 from a preliminary TCV analysis and 0D power balance; if H_NA ≈ 1, a full 40+ MW auxiliary heating system (~$100–500M) is required",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "TF coil cost dominates plant economics (~44% of MANTA's $3.4B) — NT-specific advantages address only secondary cost categories and cannot overcome the magnet cost floor",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Firefly Fusion has disclosed no proprietary plasma parameters, blanket design, tritium cycle, or power conversion approach; all company-specific analysis relies on MANTA as proxy",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "FLiBe-to-molten-salt heat exchanger is explicitly flagged by MANTA as 'low technological readiness level' and has no commercial precedent at fusion-plant scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "NT equilibria are intrinsically less vertically stable than PT at high poloidal beta — reactor-scale passive stabilizer plate engineering validation remains open beyond Guizzo et al.'s demonstrator-scale result",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "V-4Cr-4Ti vacuum vessel has never been produced at the multi-hundred-tonne scale required; nuclear-grade supply chain is non-existent",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO tape global production (~thousands km/year) vs. 5,000+ km needed per plant creates a supply-chain volume constraint for fleet-scale deployment",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Pilot-plant capacity factor of 37% is far below the 75–90% commercial target; 15-min pulsed operation requires thermal energy storage sizing not yet characterized",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Beryllium supply (~300 t/year globally, Materion-dominated) and Li-6 enrichment (Russia/China-controlled legacy amalgam processes) create FLiBe supply-chain chokepoints at fleet scale",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "PF2 coil lifetime of ~890 MW·yr (~2 full-power-years) sets an aggressive maintenance cycle driving remote-handling demands not yet demonstrated at MANTA geometry",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium global inventory (~25–30 kg, declining at 5.5%/year) constrains startup of any D-T fleet — shared with all D-T concepts but compounds Firefly's pre-disclosure stage",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
